  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-08T09:29:39.435Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The mic output volume slider currently doesn't affect the mic's volume in Windows. This means that if you are clipping a mic, lowering the mic output volume will not make the clipping any better. If a user is told their mic is too loud, they naturally would adjust this slider. It might not be making the problem any better though, voice quality can be easily improved.",
